        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c2e250f0-d0d0-5c42-9fd8-41b74ad5c5aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gaetano Donizetti, Vincenzo Bellini, Felice Romani, Charles Nodier, Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor, Eugenio Cavallini, Gioachino Rossini, Giuseppe Verdi, Saverio Mercadante, Federico Ricci, Domenico Ronzani\n- Works: Lucrezia Borgia, Il pirata, Gemma di Vergy, Maria Stuarda, Il giuramento, Il bravo, Oberto, Un giorno di regno, Maria Padilla, Nabucco, I Lombardi alla prima crociata, Giovanna d'Arco, Estella di Murcia, Salvator Rosa, Bertram, ou le Pirate, Raimonde, L'italiana in Algeri, La Cenerentola, Il barbiere di Siviglia, La sonnambula, I puritani\n- Organizations: La Scala\n- Concepts: opera structure, world premieres, tenore di grazia, leggero tenor roles\n\nFacts:\n- Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\n- Il pirata is an opera in two acts by Vincenzo Bellini with an Italian libretto by Felice Romani.\n- Il pirata was based on the 1826 three-act mélodrame Bertram, ou le Pirate by Charles Nodier and Raimonde by Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor.\n- Eugenio Cavallini served as a conductor at La Scala and led the world premieres of Lucrezia Borgia in 1833, Gemma di Vergy in 1834, Maria Stuarda in 1835, Il giuramento in 1837, Il bravo and Oberto in 1839, Un giorno di regno in 1840, Maria Padilla in 1841, Nabucco in 1842, I Lombardi alla prima crociata in 1843, Giovanna d'Arco in 1845, Estella di Murcia in 1846, and Salvator Rosa in 1854.\n- In early 19th-century Italian opera, tenor roles were invariably leggero tenor roles.\n- Rossini tenor roles identified as leggero roles include Lindoro in L'italiana in Algeri, Don Ramiro in La Cenerentola, and Almaviva in Il barbiere di Siviglia.\n- Bellini tenor roles identified as leggero roles include Gualtiero in Il pirata, Elvino in La sonnambula, and Arturo in I puritani.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
